<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.5.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00929</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.5.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>569b8774-7792-4f33-83ba-546b8a05f3df</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
  
        <exercise id="_1b355614-2928-47aa-bdb9-b75be9a3c5e5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">Rule <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gives the monthly cost, in dollars, of using <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gigabytes of data on Company <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>’s plan. Rule <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gives the monthly cost, in dollars, of using <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gigabytes of data on Company <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>’s plan.</para>
            <para id="para-00003">The total monthly cost of a cell phone plan from Company <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> costs $10, plus $15 per gigabyte for data used. The total monthly cost from Company <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> costs $80 with unlimited data.</para>
            <para id="para-00004">Which sentence describes the meaning of the statement <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00006">It costs $40 to use 2 gigabytes of data using plan <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00007">It costs $40 to use 2 gigabytes of data using plan <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00008">It costs $2 to use 40 gigabytes of data using plan <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00009">It costs $2 to use 40 gigabytes of data using plan <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00010">Correct! It costs $40 to use 2 gigabytes of data using plan <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00011">Try again. Revisit activity 4.5.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00012">The correct answer is It costs $40 to use 2 gigabytes of data using plan <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6820dc36-de9f-4726-9ff6-1a89a1be91be" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00013">Which is less, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00014">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is less. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>70</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>80</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The phone plan from Company C is less expensive if 4 gigabytes of data are used.</para>
            <para id="para-00015">Try again. Revisit activity 4.5.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00016">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is less. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>70</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>80</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The phone plan from Company C is less expensive if 4 gigabytes of data are used.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d5ae485c-d5e3-4d18-938b-dcfc65de291c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00017">Which is less, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00018">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is less. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>80</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>85</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The phone plan from Company D is less expensive if 5 gigabytes of data are used.</para>
            <para id="para-00019">Try again. Revisit activity 4.5.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00020">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is less. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>D</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>80</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>85</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The phone plan from Company D is less expensive if 5 gigabytes of data are used.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_01b2e207-fdc0-486e-a5af-d90331a0dde9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00021">For what number <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>130</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00022">Correct!</para>
            <para id="para-00023">Try again. Revisit activities 4.5.3 – 4.5.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00024">The correct answer is 8.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_459a1487-e456-4175-987e-b7a08d4000af" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00025">Function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>G</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> takes a student’s first name for its input and gives the number of letters in the first name for its output.</para>
            <para id="para-00026">Find the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>G</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mtext>Jada</m:mtext><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00027">Correct! The name “Jada” has 4 letters.</para>
            <para id="para-00028">Try again. Revisit activity 4.5.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00029">The correct answer is the name “Jada” has 4 letters.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_50204151-83a1-409c-90d5-d32808ffbaa5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00030">Find the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>G</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mtext>Diego</m:mtext><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00031">Correct!</para>
            <para id="para-00032">Try again. Revisit activity 4.5.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00033">The correct answer is 5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="de4c36d3-4c57-41cc-8605-d9865feb2be0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00034">Is the following graph a function?</para>
            
              <media alt="The figure has an absolute value function graphed on the x y-coordinate plane. The \(x\)-axis runs from negative 6 to 6. The \(y\)-axis runs from negative 4 to 8. The vertex is at the point (0, negative 1). The line goes through the points (negative 1, 0) and (1, 0).">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_08_13_01.jpg"/>
              </media>
            
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00035">Correct! Yes, this is a function because the graph passes the vertical line test.</para>
            <para id="para-00036">Try again. Revisit activities 4.5.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00037">The correct answer is: Yes, this is a function because the graph passes the vertical line test.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d546abc7-2562-40a8-bc3c-7d3e74c54ded" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00038">Is the following graph a function?</para>
            
              <media alt="The figure has a half-circle graphed on the x y-coordinate plane. The \(x\)-axis runs from negative 6 to 6. The \(y\)-axis runs from negative 6 to 6. The curved line segment starts at the point (negative 2, 0). The line goes through the point (0, 2) and ends at the point (2, 0).">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_08_13_02.jpg"/>
              </media>
            
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00039">Correct! Yes, this is a function because the graph passes the vertical line test.</para>
            <para id="para-00040">Try again. Revisit activity 4.5.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00041">The correct answer is: Yes, this is a function because the graph passes the vertical line test.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="ff99ea32-dcd7-4674-8b3b-6b1e0ee78860" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00042">Is the following graph a function?</para>
            
              <media alt="The figure has two curved lines graphed on the x y-coordinate plane. The \(x\)-axis runs from negative 6 to 6. The \(y\)-axis runs from negative 6 to 6. The curved line on the left goes through the points (negative 2, 0), (negative 4, 5), and (negative 4, negative 5). The curved line on the right goes through the points (2, 0), (4, 5), and (4, negative 5).">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_08_13_03.jpg"/>
              </media>
            
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00043">Correct! No, this is not a function because the graph does not pass the vertical line test.</para>
            <para id="para-00044">Try again. Revisit activities 4.5.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00045">The correct answer is: No, this is not a function because the graph does not pass the vertical line test.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

    </section>
  </content></document>
